ore_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03991174485544779,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":55.5,"_gate_share_shrink":2.978048343427021,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.011333991959899658,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":81.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.03374,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":22.5,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Amerant Bancorp Inc. operates as the bank holding company for Amerant Bank, N.A. that provides banking products and services to individuals and businesses in the United States. The company offers checking, savings, business, and money market accounts; cash management services; and certificates of deposit. It also provides variable and fixed rate commercial real estate loans; owner-occupied; single-family residential; commercial; and Loans to financial institutions and acceptances, and consumer loans and overdrafts, such as automobile, personal, or loans secured by cash or securities and revolving credit card agreements. In addition, the company offers trust and estate planning products and services to high net worth customers; brokerage and investment advisory services in global capital markets; retail banking; mortgage; and wealth management and fiduciary services. Further, the company provides debit and credit cards, night depositories, direct deposits, cashier's checks, safe deposit boxes, letters of credit, wire transfer, remote deposit capture, and automated clearinghouse services; derivative instruments; and online and mobile banking, account balances, statements and other documents, online transfers and bill payment, and electronic delivery of customer statements services, as well as automated teller machines ATM, and banking by mobile devices, telephone, and mail. It also operates banking centers. The company was formerly known as Mercantil Bank Holding Corporation and changed its name to Amerant Bancorp Inc. in June 2019. Amerant Bancorp Inc. was founded in 1979 and is headquartered in Coral Gables, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Carlos  Iafigliola | President, CEO & Director | Age 48 | Compensation: $766,233 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 687 people. Revenue per employee of $639K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $188K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Amerant Bancorp Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.2B market cap on $439M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $129M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 29 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.61\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 3.4% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 14% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6852243363871262},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 43% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Price-Driven Insight from (AMTB) for Rule-Based Strategy","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/40/Price-Driven_Insight_from_AMTB_for_Rule-Based_Strategy_110926091201_1794276721.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794276721.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Amerant Bancorp (AMTB) Faces A Fresh Valuation Test On Its Cleaner Balance Sheet Story","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nyse-amtb/amerant-bancorp/news/amerant-bancorp-amtb-faces-a-fresh-valuation-test-on-its-cle","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794212576.032,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.926,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Amerant Bancorp (NYSE:AMTB) Reaches New 12-Month High \u2013 Time to Buy?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/amerant-bancorp-nyseamtb-reaches-new-12-month-high-time-to-buy.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793902259.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.784,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Earnings And Buyback Expansion Might Change The Case For Investing In Amerant Bancorp (AMTB)","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nyse-amtb/amerant-bancorp/news/earnings-and-buyback-expansion-might-change-the-case-for-inv","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793597042.922,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"Amerant Bancorp (AMTB) Posted Stronger Earnings And Buybacks, Is It Still 6% Undervalued?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"